// Regression test for issue #525: double MOD with address-width env opcode
// ORIGIN returns a 160-bit address (> 64 bits).
// MOD(0, origin) = 0, then MOD(0, origin) = 0 again.
// Bug: the second MOD leaked a garbage register value instead of 0,
// because handleDivModGeneral's dividend expression tree shared
// sub-expressions with SingleLimbBB, causing undefined virtual registers
// in MultiLimbBB after instruction selection lowering.
ORIGIN
DUP1
DUP1
PUSH0
MOD
MOD
PUSH0
MSTORE
PUSH1 0x20
PUSH0
RETURN
